{"type": "result", "session_id": "local-2a931194979468c8998ca2ad9a4f24902dd1b29807ae7cb1fc85729e6824aa17", "exit_code": 0, "text": "All 6 tests pass now. The fix was in `slugify.py`:\n\n**Root cause:** When consecutive separators (spaces, underscores, dashes) appeared in the input, each one was turned into a separate `-` character. Joining them produced runs of two or more dashes (e.g., three spaces → `\"hello---world\"`), and the single `.replace(\"--\", \"-\")` only collapsed pairs, leaving double dashes for triple+ runs (`test_collapse_runs` got `'hello--world'` instead of `'hello-world'`).\n\n**Fix applied:**\n- Added `import re`.\n- In the loop, any character that isn't alphanumeric and isn't one of `\" -_\"` now also gets treated as a separator (appended `-`), so punctuation like commas/exclamation marks become dashes too.\n- Replaced the fragile `.replace(\"--\", \"-\").replace(\"  \", \" \")` with `re.sub(r\"-+\", \"-\", result)`, which collapses **any run** of one or more consecutive dashes into a single dash.\n\nThe test file `test_slugify.py` was not modified. No third-party dependencies were added.", "tokens": {"input": 226364, "output": 14849, "total": 241213, "cache_read": 186263, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 228558, "timestamp": 1793542272307}
